<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">defense</ansi>

DOGMud uses a best-of-all defense system. When attacked, all
your available defenses are rolled simultaneously and the best
result wins. Each defense type uses different skills, costs
different resources, and has different requirements.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Defense Order ━━━</ansi>

When attacked, all available defenses are rolled and the best
result wins. Each defense uses different skills and resources:

::rows
  <ansi fg="stat">Dodge</ansi>  low stamina cost, always available
  <ansi fg="stat">Parry</ansi>  moderate stamina cost, requires a weapon
  <ansi fg="stat">Block</ansi>  highest stamina cost, requires a shield
  <ansi fg="stat">Quell</ansi>  costs conviction, answers spells that attack the mind
  <ansi fg="stat">Defy</ansi>   costs conviction, answers taunts
::

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Degrees of Success ━━━</ansi>

A defence is not all or nothing. Turn a blow aside decisively and it does
nothing at all. Only just manage it and the blow still lands, robbed of most
of its force. The better your defence reads the attack, the less of it reaches
you.

An exceptional defence does more than stop the blow. See Defense Crits under
<ansi fg="command">help combat</ansi>.

Dodge, parry and block cost stamina even when they fail. Quell and defy cost
conviction instead. Run either pool dry and the defences it pays for collapse,
which is what makes a long fight a war of attrition.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Dodge Defense ━━━</ansi>

Your first line of defense, available to everyone.

::rows
  <ansi fg="stat">Skills Used: </ansi> Unarmed Combat + Dexterity
  <ansi fg="stat">Stamina Cost: </ansi> Low
  <ansi fg="stat">Requirements: </ansi> None (always available)
::

  <ansi fg="stat">Effectiveness Reduced By:</ansi>
::list
  - Heavy armor (reduces mobility)
  - High encumbrance (too much weight)
  - Being prone (severely reduced)
::

Dodge is your bread-and-butter defense. Even heavily armored fighters rely
on dodge as their first chance to take the force out of a blow.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Parry Defense ━━━</ansi>

Use your weapon to deflect incoming attacks.

::rows
  <ansi fg="stat">Skills Used: </ansi> Weapon Combat + weapon parry rating
  <ansi fg="stat">Stamina Cost: </ansi> Moderate
  <ansi fg="stat">Requirements: </ansi> Weapon equipped in primary or offhand
::

  <ansi fg="stat">Bonuses:</ansi>
::list
  - Two-handed weapons get parry bonus
  - Can parry with either hand when dual wielding
::

  <ansi fg="stat">Penalties:</ansi>
::list
  - Being prone (noticeably reduced)
::

Parry is more stamina-intensive than dodge but can be very effective with
the right weapon. Two-handed weapons excel at parrying.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Block Defense ━━━</ansi>

Use your shield to absorb the blow.

::rows
  <ansi fg="stat">Skills Used: </ansi> Weapon Combat + shield block rating
  <ansi fg="stat">Stamina Cost: </ansi> High (most expensive defense)
  <ansi fg="stat">Requirements: </ansi> Shield equipped in offhand
::

  <ansi fg="stat">Benefits:</ansi>
::list
  - High effectiveness with quality shields
  - Works reasonably well even when prone (slightly reduced)
::

  <ansi fg="stat">Penalties:</ansi>
::list
  - Highest stamina cost
  - Cannot dual wield weapons (shield takes offhand slot)
::

Block is your final defense layer. Shields are stamina-hungry but provide
excellent protection when your other defenses fail.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Defense Strategy ━━━</ansi>

  <ansi fg="stat">Stamina Management:</ansi>
  Long fights drain stamina quickly. Each dodge, parry, or block
  attempt costs stamina, so manage your pool carefully. Low stamina
  imposes severe combat penalties.

  <ansi fg="stat">Equipment Choices:</ansi>
::list
  - Dual wield: More attacks, only dodge and parry
  - Sword + Shield: Fewer attacks, all three defenses
  - Two-handed weapon: Moderate attacks, strong parry, no block
::

  <ansi fg="stat">While Prone:</ansi>
  All defenses are severely reduced when knocked down, and attacks against
  you land harder. Getting up matters more than anything else you could be
  doing.

  You try to rise on your own after a moment, but that is no longer a
  certainty: if an enemy is standing over you, the two of you contest it,
  and a stronger opponent can keep you down. Nobody is held forever, and
  fighting your way back up teaches you something either way.

  <ansi fg="command">stand</ansi> is the guaranteed way out. It costs stamina and it always
  works, however badly you are being held. If you are down and want out
  now, use it rather than waiting.

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Counterattacks ━━━</ansi>

A defense does not only spare you damage. Defend decisively enough and
your opponent leaves an opening:

::list
  - A decisive dodge, parry or block earns a free answering swing the
    attacker must defend in turn, at reduced damage. A decisive quell
    earns the same.
  - A decisive defy answers with words instead: a retort that wounds
    the other side's nerve, whether they taunted you or tried to charm
    you.
::

You do not choose this and it costs you no action. It falls out of
defending well, which is another reason to carry defenses you can
actually use.

Two things worth knowing:

::list
  - Every attack channel can be answered, not just weapons.
  - Reach and aim decide it. Someone shooting you from another room
    cannot be answered, because you cannot reach them. A working or a
    sweep that reaches everyone in the room earns no answer either: the
    free strike is for an attack aimed at you alone.
::

<ansi fg="yellow">━━━ Defense Skills ━━━</ansi>

Improve your defenses by progressing these skills:

::rows
  <ansi fg="stat">Unarmed Combat: </ansi> Improves dodge effectiveness
  <ansi fg="stat">Weapon Combat: </ansi> Improves parry and block effectiveness
  <ansi fg="stat">Dexterity Stat: </ansi> Improves dodge chance (use-based progression)
::

Train these skills through combat and see your survivability increase
dramatically.

